        <detaileddescription>
<para>Generate a random sample from the Random-Effects Normal distribution.</para><para>Generate <computeroutput>N</computeroutput> independent draws from <formula id="2">$p(\boldsymbol{\mu} \mid \boldsymbol{x})$</formula>, where <formula id="3">\[ \begin{aligned} \boldsymbol{\mu} &amp; \sim \mathcal N(\boldsymbol{\lambda}, \boldsymbol{\Sigma}) \\ \boldsymbol{x} \mid \boldsymbol{\mu} &amp; \sim \mathcal N(\boldsymbol{\mu}, \boldsymbol{V}). \end{aligned} \]</formula> Each argument can be vectorized, meaning that it can have length either <computeroutput>N</computeroutput> or <computeroutput>1</computeroutput>, denoted here as <computeroutput>n</computeroutput>.</para><para><parameterlist kind="param"><parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername direction="in">N</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>Integer number of random draws. </para></parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername direction="in">x</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>Matrix of size <computeroutput>q x n</computeroutput> of observations. </para></parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername direction="in">V</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>Matrix of size <computeroutput>q x nq</computeroutput> of observation variances. </para></parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername direction="in">lambda</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>Matrix of size <computeroutput>q x n</computeroutput> of prior means. </para></parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername direction="in">Sigma</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>Matrix of size <computeroutput>q x nq</computeroutput> of prior variances.</para></parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
</parameterlist>
<simplesect kind="return"><para>Matrix of size <computeroutput>q x Nq</computeroutput> of random draws of observation means <computeroutput>mu</computeroutput>. </para></simplesect>
</para>        </detaileddescription>
